{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310617,"nonce":"TSYXJ4/Z1LBR08JvSgUEqRPShwc=","title":"OPEN — a plain function used as a VALUE is wrapped as {fn_ptr, null_env} but CallIndirect always prepends env, so a static callee reads the ...","message":"**MINIMAL REPRO (deterministic SIGSEGV, both macOS arm64 and Linux x86-64):**\n```haxe\nclass L1 {\n  static function g(b:Bool) return b ? 1 : -1;\n  static function main() {\n    var c = (function(f) { return function(b) { return f(b); }; })(g);\n    Sys.println(\"L1=\" + c(true));   // SIGSEGV, fault=0x1\n  }\n}\n```\n`/tmp/lad/L1.hx`. L3 (capture fn + anon, forward two args) and L4 (Int instead\nof Bool) crash the same way; L2 (capture an anon, no function capture) prints\n`null` instead of crashing.\n\n**THE DEFECT.** `mir/expr/variables.rs` (~line 103) lowers a function used as a\nVALUE to `FunctionRef`, which `cranelift_backend.rs` wraps as\n`{fn_ptr, env_ptr = null}` — its comment says CallIndirect \"unifies on closure\nobjects\". But `CallIndirect` then ALWAYS does `call_args.insert(0, env_ptr)`,\nwhile the referenced function is a plain static with NO env parameter. So\n`f(b)` through the closure reaches `g(null, b)`: a one-parameter `g` reads the\nnull env as its argument. `b` reads false ⇒ **the `1 != -1` half of Issue6480**;\nwith more parameters the whole argument list shifts ⇒ the crash.\n\nCLIF proof, inner lambda: `v7` is the captured value, then\n`v8 = load v7`, `v9 = load v7+8`, `call_indirect sig0, v8(v9, v1)`.\n\n**FIXED 2026-09-09 in 5e40a9ed** by `ensure_closure_value_adapter`\n(mir/decl/vtables.rs): an adapter with the ERASED signature\n`(env: *u8, i64..) -\u003e i64` that unboxes each argument to what the callee\ndeclares (`haxe_unbox_scalar_or_addr`) and BOXES a scalar result back --\nthe caller reads the result as a Dynamic and hands it to\n`haxe_std_string_ptr`, so a raw `1` was dereferenced as an address. The\nreturn half was the piece the first attempt missed: after fixing only the\narguments, `b=true` arrived correctly and the crash MOVED to the return.\nResult: L1/L3/L4/F all answer correctly; Issue6480 12/12 PASS on Linux\n(was 4 of 8); corpus 495 on macOS unchanged, 496 on the NUC.\n\n**ATTEMPT 1 REVERTED (2026-09-09).** Referencing an env-absorbing thunk at that\nsite instead of the raw function — `ensure_vtable_dispatch_thunk(func_id)`,\nwhich builds exactly `(env, params..) -\u003e ret`. The thunk IS emitted and\nreferenced (`__vtable_dispatch_thunk__L1_g`, CLIF `(i64, i8) -\u003e i32`), but L1\nstill crashes and the corpus went 495 -\u003e 494 (0 gained, and the \"loss\" was\nIssue6480 landing the other way). **A SECOND LAYER remains:** the call site\nstill declares the erased `sig0 = (i64, i64) -\u003e i64` rather than the callee's\nreal signature, and the `Bool` arrives BOXED (`haxe_box_bool_ptr`) because the\nlambda's parameter is erased to `*void`. Fixing the env alone cannot work until\nthe call site's signature and the boxed argument agree with the callee.\n\n**FLAKE MAP (corrected — do not call all three \"known bistable\"):** on Linux,\nserial, 8 runs each — Issue6480 4 PASS/4 WRONG (the ONLY genuinely bistable\nrow, and what separates CI's 494 from a local 495); Issue3635 8/8 PASS\n(a macOS-ONLY flake); Issue4675 8/8 CRASH (a STABLE failure, not noise);\nIssue10752 consistently CRASH.\n\n**MEMORY SENSITIVITY IS REAL.** On the 16 GB Mac, Issue6480 passes 12/12 run\nserially and unloaded, and fails 4/12 under `nue/bench/ballast.py 6 90 churn`.\nThe 6 GB NUC reproduces it with no ballast at all, which makes\n[[feedback_use_nuc_not_local_vms_for_linux]] the right box for this class of\nbug — it matches CI's platform and keeps the load off the laptop.\n\nNUC has the branch `conf-flake` built with the corpus fetched (pushed over ssh\nto `nuc:/home/raikage/rayzor`, not to GitHub).\n\nRelated: [[bugs_devirtualizer_dropped_closure_env]] (same family, different\nshape — that one was the devirtualizer, this one is the base lowering).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_function_as_value_gets_an_env_it_has_no_param_for` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}